traceability: section {
  | Which test or script proves each requirement of the spec. The links are kept apart from
  | the spec, which names no tests:
  |
  | - [the traceability](#traceability) holds a `proves(…)` per spec requirement, with the
  |   `verify(path, test)` of each test that proves it, one page per area of the spec;
  | - [the status](#status) lists the requirements no test proves yet, as planned or untested;
  | - each component's invariants carry their own `verify`, and the done criteria of
  |   [unit 1](#delivery.unit_1) and [unit 2](#delivery.unit_2) are `verify` links on the components they exercise.
  |
  | `heron generate conformance` writes the report of all three to
  | `.heron/conformance/`: each requirement proven, planned, untested or missing.
}
